WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
- What makes you an artist

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.930
is that you wake up in the morning

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.692
and you have this creative
energy to produce.

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:07.540
(synth music)

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.460
Dubai has become a magnet
for the most eclectic

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.650
and talented creative minds.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.360
If I could sum it up in one word,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.575
I would say potential.

00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:21.408
(cheerful piano music)

00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:22.410
- I'm Anna Devis.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.300
- I'm Daniel Rueda.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.160
- Together, we are
architects and photographers.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.200
- Our approach is to play
with perspectives and geometry

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.930
within an urban landscape.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.040
- And as architects,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:33.910
we travel the world,

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.280
exploring and seeing aspects of buildings.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.133
So we can tell stories to the image.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.330
- We are on a journey to
meet with other like-minded

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.631
and inspiring creatives in Dubai.

00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:46.214
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.207
- We are exploring
Dubai's foremost art hub,

00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:52.680
Alserkal Avenue.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.600
Bringing together established
gallery exhibitions,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.680
workshops, and studios
where grassroots artists

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.030
are given the tools to begin creating.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.480
- To learn how it came to be,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.034
we meet with the Director
of Alserkal Avenue.

00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:05.867
- Welcome.

00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.550
- I'm originally from Lithuania.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.730
I studied in the States
and then in London.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.090
And then the last stop was Dubai.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.590
- I'm looking forward for
us to kind of walk around

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.350
and introduce you to the
creative community of Dubai.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.553
- Alserkal Avenue is
comprised of ninety-one

00:01:21.553 --> 00:01:23.620
different warehouses.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.140
It used to be an old marble factory

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.153
that belonged to Alserkal family.

00:01:30.592 --> 00:01:33.240
- I wanted to make a
meaningful contribution

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.680
to arts and culture.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.570
For me, Alserkal Avenue is about bringing

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.870
the community closer to arts and culture

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:44.639
through a variety of art
forms and experiences.

00:01:44.639 --> 00:01:46.740
(upbeat music)

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.310
- The art scene is just taking its steps

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.650
and just starting to create itself.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.840
It's so important that there is someone

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.770
that believes in a young artist.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.003
There's an incredible homegrown
artistic community here.

00:02:00.003 --> 00:02:03.300
And really, really talented individuals

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.180
that are involved in creating the history

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.310
and really producing fantastic work,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.773
that's now becoming more
recognized internationally.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.010
- Hi. We saw the workshop from outside

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.060
and we're curious about what you guys do.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.150
- We're here doing sneaker customization.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.450
- How does it feel to
be working in this space

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.390
with all this art around you?

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.223
- It's really good.

00:02:26.223 --> 00:02:27.640
It's inspiring for us as artists

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.290
because once you arrive in Dubai

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.860
it feels like everything
is super polished.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.330
Once you get to know the creative scene

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.740
you realize that you can
do whatever you want to,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.380
just need to find the
right place to do it.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.960
- To date, we've worked with almost twenty

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.570
artists from all over the world.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.600
And so you feel that step by step

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.460
we are building the
infrastructure for the arts.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.370
Not only for the city of Dubai

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:51.980
but for the UAE and the region.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.066
In the past we produced
about three thousand

00:02:55.066 --> 00:02:58.050
cultural events open
and free to the public,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:02.670
anything from music to film
screening to an exhibition.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.010
And as a result, we saw
a rise in our community.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.341
- We had the pleasure to
meet with local artist,

00:03:09.341 --> 00:03:12.630
Shaika Al Mazrou, who was
exhibiting her intriguing

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.050
debut works "Expansion/Extension."

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.170
Shaika's challenging the
perception of the types

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.460
of artwork one might expect to find

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.020
coming out of Dubai.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.430
- I always tend to say this.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.900
When you're comfortable you tend

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.420
to make boring works.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.750
And I like to push myself in this

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.400
kind of uncomfortable corner.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.500
So these come in metal sheets.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.890
I see this material and I really

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.800
want to change their physical properties.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.780
You start, you know, squeezing it,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.100
changing its norms.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.920
- So funny how you use the word "squeeze"

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.378
when you're speaking about metal,

00:03:42.378 --> 00:03:44.090
which is not a squeezable material,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.433
so that's amazing.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.060
- Next, we visit JPNF collection.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.790
- A private museum bringing decades

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.483
of experienced artist
prowess to Alserkal Avenue.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.470
- We're very proud of our space.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:00.730
It is really designed
with abstract art in mind.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.920
Every decision an artist makes affects

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.512
the results of their work.

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:06.345
- Totally.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.510
- So whether it is the
shape of the canvas,

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.800
size of their brush,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.660
- Everything has a
thought behind it, right?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.493
- Absolutely.

00:04:13.493 --> 00:04:14.810
- We kind of relate also.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.490
We have this super simple images

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.800
but at the same time you have
all the work done before.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.020
- It's so important to constantly

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.270
embrace the history of the context

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.450
and the local elements before we're able

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.300
to create a story of our own.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.040
- These local artists are proud

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.210
of where they've come from

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.360
and clearly see where they are going.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.810
To be able to meet with
these inspiring artists

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.750
felt like we were
discovering the beginning

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.896
of something special in
Dubai's artistic scene.

00:04:42.896 --> 00:04:44.040
(upbeat music)

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.050
- When it comes to creative talent,

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.827
it's so important to create a platform

00:04:48.827 --> 00:04:52.540
and the springboard where
their work to be shown.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.830
It's this access to opportunity

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:57.420
and potential to realize anything

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.853
that you set out to do.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.703
And I think a city like
Dubai allows you to do that.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.123
(upbeat music)

